"The Everything Shop" is a functional e-commerce web application developed as a semester project for the Object-Oriented Analysis and Design course.

The primary goal of this project is to apply theoretical knowledge of software engineering to build a complete Model-View-Controller (MVC) system. The application allows users to browse products, manage a shopping cart, and place orders. It allows administrators to manage products and view orders.

The system is built using the PERN stack (PostgreSQL, Express, React, Node.js) with TypeScript, ensuring type safety and code maintainability. Docker is used to containerize the application for consistent development environments.

This report documents the analysis, design, and implementation of the system, highlighting the practical application of design patterns and web development best practices.
